# BlockML xmlns prefix convention

**Rule of thumb:** short prefix = BlockML. Domain mirrors use a domain token (`mb` for MachineBlocks).

If you read `core:`, `type:`, `unit:`, or `lang:` it is always `org.blockml.bml.*` — no lookup.

## BlockML (`org.blockml.bml.*`)

| Prefix | Package |
|--------|---------|
| `blockml` | `org.blockml.bml` |
| `core` | `org.blockml.bml.core` |
| `type` | `org.blockml.bml.type` |
| `unit` | `org.blockml.bml.unit` |
| `lang` | `org.blockml.bml.language` |
| `def` | `org.blockml.bml.definition` |
| `constraint` / `status` / `validation` / … | matching package segment |
| `bml` | `org.blockml.bml.annotation.BmlAnnotation` |
| `ann` | `org.blockml.bml.annotation` |

Do **not** use legacy `bcore` / `btype`.

## MachineBlocks domain (`com.machineblocks.bml.*`)

| Prefix | Package |
|--------|---------|
| `mb` | `com.machineblocks.bml` |
| `mbcore` | `com.machineblocks.bml.core` |
| `mbtype` | `com.machineblocks.bml.type` |
| `mbunit` | `com.machineblocks.bml.unit` |
| `mbann` | `com.machineblocks.bml.annotation` |
| `scad` | `…annotation.ScadAnnotation` |
| `bricks` / `cal` / `examples` | collective packages |

```xml
<!-- ❌ BAD — steals BlockML aliases -->
xmlns:core="com.machineblocks.bml.core"
xmlns:type="com.machineblocks.bml.type"

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
xmlns:mbcore="com.machineblocks.bml.core"
xmlns:mbtype="com.machineblocks.bml.type"
```

See also `blockml-xmlns-ordering.mdc` (attribute order) and `docs/02_mbml.md` — § XML prefix convention.
